  "query_preview": "..\n\nLatest water vapor shows dry mid levels over southeast Michigan, \nwhich is also confirmed by the 00z DTX RAOB, which indicated a 700 \nMB dew pt depression of 20 C with a PW value of 0.59 inches. This \ndry air mass will hold today, although patchy ground fog looks to be \naround to start the day. Return flow around the departing high \npressure will increase this evening and tonight. A shortwave over \nMissouri will shear off to the northeast today and mainly track \nthrough the eastern Great Lakes Saturday morning. Still, sufficient \nmoisture tracking into eastern half of the CWA, along with enough \ndestabilization (slightly negative LI's and MLcape of 750+ J/kg), \nwill support the potential for isolated showers and thunderstorms \n(see 00z HRRR/RRFS). A secondary moisture axis out ahead of a cold \nfront will also track in from the western Great Lakes late in the \nday, passing through during the evening or washing out altogether. \nThe bulk of the shower activity is expected to reside over Lake \nHuron however.\n\nWith cooler cyclonic flow on Sunday, its still not out of the \nquestion for isolated light showers before a mid level dry slot \nbecomes fully established over southern Michigan. 850 MB temps \ndropping into the mid single numbers Sunday night will bring \npotential for mins in the 40s as high pressure builds over the \nregion. The wild card is whether low clouds develop with the light \nonshore flow off the warm waters of Lake Huron. \n\nA strong storm system will track through the northern Plains on \nMonday and into northwest Ontario Monday night. The active warm \nfront is expected to reside over western Great Lakes. Warm air will \neject out of the southern Plains, with the 00z Euro indicating 850 \nMB temps warming to 20 C; setting up Tuesday as sneaky warm day \nahead of cold front. Timing of FROPA and extent of cloud cover and \nshowers is uncertain, but high temperatures in the 80s seems \nreasonable. Mid level frontogenesis hanging around Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday will offer up a continued good chance of rain.",
